menu "RID receiver"

    config RID_CAPTURE_CHANNEL
        int "2.4 GHz capture channel"
        default 6
        range 1 13
        help
            Channel 6 is the RID Beacon default. A Windows Wi-Fi Direct
            bench transmitter chooses its own channel (11 on the tested
            MT7612U); set this to match it.

    config RID_SCAN_DWELL_MS
        int "Channel hop dwell time (ms, 0 = stay on the capture channel)"
        default 0
        range 0 5000
        help
            0 stays on RID_CAPTURE_CHANNEL. A non-zero value hops
            1 -> 6 -> 11, staying this long on each, to find a source on
            an unknown channel. Each hop is an SDIO round trip to the C6,
            so frames are lost while hopping; use it only to locate a
            source, then fix the channel.

    config RID_DEBUG_WATCH_MAC
        string "Log every management frame from this MAC (bench debug)"
        default ""
        help
            Colon-separated MAC address, for example 06:13:ef:3f:65:d5.
            Matching Beacons and Probe Responses are printed as RID_WATCH
            lines with channel, RSSI and element IDs, whether or not they
            carry RID. Leave empty to disable.

endmenu
